# ============================================================
#  THE HOLLOW STAR: Acts II-IV as arc beats (arc: hollowstar)
#
#  Act II (investigation, year 2): the Wardens stir.
#    beat 4  hs_silver_rings, hs_seraphine_towers
#    beat 5  hs_frost_ring
#  Act III (escalation, year 3): a tower goes dark, sides are taken.
#    beat 7  hs_dark_tower (may advance the clock to 8), hs_maud_locks
#    beat 8  hs_choosing_sides -> flag sided_wardens | sided_dumonts | sided_self
#  Act IV (convergence, year 4): preparation before the summons.
#    beat 10 hs_last_winter, hs_ilse_door
#  Preparation (key clues, allies at rel >= 30, the side flag) sets
#  the tier of the seal challenge in hs_beneath.
# ============================================================

# ---------------- Act II: the Wardens stir ----------------

@event hs_silver_rings
title: Silver at Supper
arc: hollowstar
beat: 4
slot: night
class: story
tone: eerie
art: ring
tags: mystery hollowstar
chain: hollowstar
scene: The Great Hall at supper, candlelight catching three identical silver rings on three very different hands at the high table.
text: At supper you notice three identical silver rings at the high table: on the headmistress, on Professor Thorne and on Old Maud's earthy hand. After curfew, from your window, you see all three walking the lakeshore with lanterns, stopping at the foot of each tower in turn.
> left: Follow them down
  challenge deceive medium:
    win:
      hollow +1
      lore +small
      say: You shadow them from tower to tower. At each one they lay a palm on the stone and wait. At the last, Maud takes her hand away and blows on her fingers as if the wall were ice.
    lose:
      mood -small
      rel thorne -small
      say: A lantern swings toward you. "Hm," says Professor Thorne. "Bed." He doesn't report you, which somehow feels worse.
> right: Draw the curtains
  health +small
  mood -tiny
  say: You sleep well, mostly. In the morning the rings are still there at breakfast, and nobody at the high table looks as if they slept at all.

@event hs_seraphine_towers
title: Seven, Then Six
arc: hollowstar
beat: 4
slot: night
class: story
tone: eerie
actor: seraphine
art: tower
tags: mystery hollowstar
chain: hollowstar
scene: A seer on the observatory balcony at night, counting the academy's towers on her fingers, one finger held back.
text: Seraphine is on the observatory balcony, counting towers on her fingers. "Seven," she says. "Seven. Six, and then… no. Seven, for now." She looks at you as if you had arrived a little early. "What month is it? I lose track around the… you know."
> left: "Which one goes out?"
  hollow +1
  lore +small
  mood -small
  say: She points, then frowns at her own hand. "That one. Or the one next to it. Next year, I think." She doesn't remember saying it the next morning, but you do.
> right: "It's {month}. Evening."
  rel seraphine +medium
  mood +tiny
  say: She lets out a long breath and sits down on the cold stone. "Thank you. I was halfway into a winter." You stay until she is sure which one she's in.

@event hs_frost_ring
title: A Ring of Frost
arc: hollowstar
beat: 5
slot: night
class: story
tone: tense
art: snow
tags: mystery hollowstar
chain: hollowstar
scene: The Mirror Lake on a warm spring night, a perfect white ring of frost on the water, a tall woman standing at the waterline with a lantern.
text: A warm night, and a ring of frost has formed in the middle of the lake: perfectly round, perfectly white, as wide as the Great Hall. Far below it, very faintly, a bell tolls once. The headmistress is standing alone at the waterline.
> left: Watch what she does
  challenge deceive medium:
    win:
      hollow +1
      find lake_bell
      lore +small
      say: She kneels and speaks to the water, slow and patient, the way you would speak to a sleeping animal. The ring shrinks, cracks, and is gone. She stays kneeling a long time afterwards.
    lose:
      rel isolde +tiny
      mood -small
      say: "Good evening," she says, without turning round. "You are the third student this week. The other two asked questions." She tells you nothing, and remembers your name.
> right: Stay inside
  mood -small
  health +tiny
  say: You stay inside with the shutters closed. By morning the lake is blue and glittering, and the first-years are already arguing about whether anyone saw anything at all.

# ---------------- Act III: escalation ----------------

@event hs_dark_tower
title: The Tower That Went Dark
arc: hollowstar
beat: 7
class: story
tone: grim
art: candle
tags: mystery hollowstar danger
chain: hollowstar
scene: An academy tower standing black against the night sky among its lit neighbours, and below it a lake half-covered in autumn ice.
text: Mid-lecture, every lamp in the Lecture Tower goes out at once, and none of them will light again. Nobody is hurt. By morning, weeks before any frost, half the lake has frozen: a sheet of ice that ends in a clean edge, as if cut. The prefects are already telling everyone to keep off it.
> left: Walk out onto the ice
  challenge research medium:
    win:
      hollow +1
      advance hollowstar +1
      lore +medium
      health -small
      say: Under your boots the ice is clear as glass. Far down, something round and dark sits on the lakebed, and a faint glow runs along its rim. Then the glow turns, slowly, as if to look up.
    lose:
      health -medium
      say: The ice groans and a crack races past your feet. You scramble back to the shore soaked to the knee, and a prefect writes your name down very slowly.
> right: Carry lamps for the prefects
  renown +small
  health -tiny
  say: You spend the night carrying lamps up the Lecture Tower stairs. Every one goes out at the doorway. From her window across the courtyard, the headmistress watches you try.

@event hs_maud_locks
title: Maud Has Seen Ice Before
arc: hollowstar
beat: 7
when: seen(hs_dark_tower) > 0
class: story
tone: eerie
actor: maud
art: cup
tags: mystery hollowstar
chain: hollowstar
scene: An old woman wrapped in a shawl on her cottage step, two mugs steaming beside her, looking down at a half-frozen lake.
text: Maud is on her cottage step with two mugs of tea, as if she expected you. "The lake doesn't freeze this time of year, dearie," she says. "Last time it froze at all, I lost a friend to it." She pushes a mug toward you. "Sit. Or ask. You can't really do both."
> left: Sit with her
  rel maud +medium
  mood -tiny
  say: You drink your tea and watch the ice. She hums something old. When the mugs are empty she squeezes your hand. "That was the right one," she says, and you'll only understand why much later.
> right: Ask what's holding it shut
  hollow +1
  find seven_locks
  rel maud +small
  mood -small
  say: "Seven towers, seven locks, one in each," she says. "When a tower goes quiet, so does its lock." She looks at the dark tower. "Locks can be mended. They need hands, and they need a key."

@event hs_choosing_sides
title: Two Invitations
arc: hollowstar
beat: 8
when: hollow >= 2 or flag(kael_told) or flag(warden_trial)
type: menu
class: story
tone: tense
art: letter
tags: mystery hollowstar
chain: hollowstar
scene: A student holding two folded notes, one sealed in silver wax and one in frost, standing between a tower and a boathouse.
text: Two invitations in one day. A note in the headmistress's neat hand: "My study, after supper. Come alone. There will be chess." And Kael, waiting at the boathouse: "She wants you in her circle. I know the door from the other side." He looks at the dark tower. "Come with us. If you want."
> wardens: Join the headmistress's circle
  hint: The Wardens: old rules, old wards.
  flag sided_wardens
  rel isolde +large
  rel kael -small
  lore +small
  say: She beats you at chess in eleven moves, then tells you about the seal while she resets the board. "Rings are for people who have stood on the ice," she says. "Until then, you have my door."
> dumonts: Stand with the Dumonts
  hint: Kael's way, against his own family.
  flag sided_dumonts
  rel kael +large
  rel isolde -small
  if met(ilse):
    rel ilse +small
  arcana +small
  say: "Not my family," Kael says. "Us." He teaches you to hold a ward in a wind that wants your fingers. His hands are cold. They are steadier than yours.
> self: Go my own way
  hint: Nobody's circle. Nobody's help.
  flag sided_self
  guile +small
  lore +small
  mood -small
  say: You thank them both and keep your own notes in your own cipher. It's lonelier than you expected. Both of them, you notice, keep an eye on you anyway.
> none: Stay out of it
  hint: It isn't your door.
  mood +small
  rel kael -tiny
  say: You turn both invitations down. Kael nods as if he expected it. The headmistress's note simply says, the next morning, "Understood. Mind the ice."

# ---------------- Act IV: convergence ----------------

@event hs_last_winter
title: The Last Winter Before
arc: hollowstar
beat: 10
when: hollow >= 2 or flag(sided_wardens) or flag(sided_dumonts) or flag(sided_self)
type: menu
class: story
tone: tense
art: lantern
tags: mystery hollowstar
chain: hollowstar
scene: Lantern light in a frost-rimed window, the frozen edge of the lake beyond it, a student's desk covered in maps of seven towers.
text: The Lecture Tower has been dark for a year, and the lake has started freezing overnight in strange shapes: circles, mostly. Everyone who knows what's under it is getting ready in their own way. You have one winter and not enough evenings. Who do you spend them with?
> kael: Train with Kael on the ice
  rel kael +large
  health -small
  say: He drills you on the ice until you can hold a ward with numb hands. "Again," he says, and then, quietly, "Good." You will remember that he said it.
> maud: Mend wards with Maud
  rel maud +large
  mood -small
  say: You walk the towers with her, tracing old wards back into the stone. "Your hands are steadier than mine were," she says, and doesn't say whose hands she means.
> isolde: Study with the headmistress
  rel isolde +large
  lore +small
  mood -small
  say: You lose at chess every evening and learn the founders' words between moves. Once you nearly win. Her short, delighted laugh is the warmest sound you hear all winter.
> ilse: Spar with Ilse at the shore
  when: met(ilse) and not flag(ilse_taken) and not flag(ilse_went_north)
  rel ilse +large
  health -small
  say: She knocks you into the snow eleven times. The twelfth time you don't fall, and she looks at you as if you had done a trick she has never learned the counter to.
> alone: Rest while you still can
  hint: A quiet winter. Nobody else's.
  rest
  say: You sleep, you eat, you read novels with no doors in them. It's the kindest winter you've had in years, and you can feel the lake getting colder anyway.

@event hs_ilse_door
title: What Ilse Was Taught
arc: hollowstar
beat: 10
when: met(ilse) and not clue(ilse_truth) and not flag(ilse_taken) and not flag(ilse_went_north)
actor: ilse
class: story
tone: grim
art: door
tags: mystery hollowstar
chain: hollowstar
scene: A young woman in white furs drawing a round door in the snow with the tip of a wand, a frozen lake behind her.
text: Ilse draws a circle in the snow with her wand, then a smaller one inside it. "This is the door," she says. "I have drawn it every day since I was six. I have never seen it." She doesn't look up. "Ask me what they taught me to do. Or don't. I don't care which."
> left: "What did they teach you?"
  find ilse_truth
  hollow +1
  rel ilse +small
  mood -small
  say: She tells you, flatly, like a lesson recited: how to stand, what to say, where to put her hands. "They raised me to open it," she says. "Nobody asked me if I wanted to." Then, sharply: "Now you know. Don't look at me like that."
> right: "You don't have to tell me."
  rel ilse +medium
  mood -tiny
  say: She rubs the circle out with her boot. "Kindness," she says, as if naming a trick. "I haven't learned the counter to that one yet." She doesn't leave, though.
